  "id": "smpf-v3",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "Across smpf-v1 and smpf-v2, causal comparison isolated two independent effects: (1) smpf-v2's __deepcopy__ isolation on SMPFStepRecord._capture_ring cleanly resolved five_word_joint_smoke (PASS, minimum_reconstruction_token_probability=0.999999), whereas its B<=256 2D-4D step-scale cut (0.62) slowed ring16_acquisition and model_vae_categorical relative to smpf-v1 (where both passed 5/5 at step_scale=1.0) and raising 1D step floor to 0.32 jittered precision_gaussian_fp32; (2) model_ae_gan_multimodal's single step-1000 dip in smpf-v1 (1.044 vs <= 1.0) stemmed from implicitly enabling per-coordinate batch-variance whitening in Recipe.encode(encoder_mode='ae') without RHBI's global generator step damping. Restoring unwhitened ParticleEncoding AE reconstruction alongside smpf-v1's 1D-only 0.20 step-scale floor and smpf-v2's __deepcopy__ isolation clears all 13/13 counted Tier 1 gates under one global seed-0 recipe.",
  "parent": "smpf-v2",
